/* ============================ works: one canonical list ====================
   Thompson's printed *Bibliography and Abbreviations* (transcribed from the
   Missouri LibGuide) and the abbreviations the text actually cites are two
   views of the same shelf: 504 of the 637 printed heads are cited under
   exactly that key.  They used to be two pages, so most rows appeared twice.
   Now there is one list, keyed by abbreviation:
     - a printed head may carry several works (Frazer has seven); they are
       listed under one abbreviation instead of repeating it;
     - the full text no longer repeats the abbreviation it is filed under
       ("AA n.s. = American Anthropologist…" prints as "American…");
     - abbreviations the text cites but the printed list does not contain are
       marked as such rather than showing up on a second page. */
